# White Label page sync (`whitelabel/flightdealio-wl.html`)

`flights.flightdealio.com` is **not** a Next.js route. It is Travelpayouts White Label HTML stored in this repo as:

`whitelabel/flightdealio-wl.html`

Treat that file as a **real product page** (header/nav, brand, theme, Google tag).

## When you must update it

If you change any of the following on the **main site**, update the White Label HTML to match:

- Header / logo / nav links (Flights, Stays, Taxi, eSIM, future menu items)
- Brand name, colors, hero feel
- Theme switcher behavior (`theme_choice` localStorage)
- Google Ads gtag ID / conversion `send_to` label

Preserve all Travelpayouts placeholders and mounts:

- `[:embed_script:]`, `[:cookie_policy_script:]`, `[:og_image:]`, `[:route_info:]`, `[:current_year:]`, `[:widget_domain:]`
- `#tpwl-search`, `#tpwl-tickets`, `#tpwl-widget-weedles`, cookie banner markup

## After editing

Always tell the user to **re-paste the file into Travelpayouts → White Label → Edit → Custom HTML → Save**, then hard-refresh `https://flights.flightdealio.com`.
